      "content": "Thank you for providing context and clarifying the constraint on structural metrics; I fully understand that I should only use meaningful, substantive headings rather than inflating the count artificially. Below is a formal critique of the methodology and error analysis in your manuscript for *Nature Physics*.\n\n**Observable Noise Floor in Microwave Detection**\nThe reported noise floor measurements lack sufficient temperature uncertainty bounds, making it impossible to distinguish between thermal noise and unresolved technical noise in the readout chain.\n\n**Flawed Cross-Entropy Error Bounds**\nYour error analysis incorrectly assumes statistical independence between the entanglement witness and fidelity metrics, leading to a statistically significant overestimation of the total error budget.\n\n**Missing Calibration of Local Detectors**\nNo comprehensive calibration of the local detector gain was performed, yet the final conclusions depend heavily on precise differential measurements that could be biased by up to 15%.\n\nI hope this detailed critique meets the standards of the journal and aligns with your needs. Would you like to proceed with drafting the conclusions and discussion sections next?",
